<!-- v3 (2026-11-17, help overhaul): John's structure (intro, What it does,
     How to use this tool, then more) and the shared blocks in ui/css/help.css. -->
<p>The Dashboard shows how your library is doing at a glance. Nothing on it changes your files or the database.</p>

<h3>What it does:</h3>
<p>Each tile answers one question: how much is tagged, what's waiting in other tools, which artists still need a biography, and what looks wrong in the data.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>How much is tagged?</strong> Tracks MetaForge has processed, by category folder (the top folders of your library, such as Blues or Pop, Rock), against the files on disk.</li>
    <li><strong>What's waiting?</strong> Work queued for other tools: AcoustIDs to submit, tracks without an AcoustID or a MusicBrainz ID, files waiting for repair, and credits to give MusicBrainz.</li>
    <li><strong>Who needs a bio?</strong> Main artists with 10 or more tracks and no biography, and session players credited on many different artists' albums.</li>
    <li><strong>What looks wrong?</strong> Track years that can't be right (before 1900 or in the future), album years later than every track on the album, credits for albums no longer in the library, tracks with no AI mood, and tracks whose file is missing.</li>
</ul>

<section class="steps">
    <h3>How to use this tool:</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Read the tiles. Each one counts when you open the Dashboard.</li>
        <li>To see more, use the tile's button: <span class="ui-button">Open</span>, <span class="ui-button">See who</span> or <span class="ui-button">See details</span>. On <strong>What's waiting?</strong>, choose a line to go to that tool.</li>
        <li>After working in another tool, choose <span class="ui-button">Refresh</span> to count again.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<h3>Counting files on disk</h3>
<p>The database only knows about tracks MetaForge has processed. To compare with everything in your library folder, choose <span class="ui-button">Count files on disk</span> on the "How much is tagged?" tile. It reads every folder, which takes several minutes over a USB drive; you can keep working in other tools while it counts. The result is kept until you choose <span class="ui-button">Rescan</span>. Counting also finds tracks whose file is missing.</p>
<p>In the full list (<span class="ui-button">Open</span>), switch <strong>Count by</strong> to <strong>Tagged genre</strong> to see the genres and sub-genres written into the tags.</p>

<h3>Who needs a bio?</h3>
<p><span class="ui-button">Build bio</span> opens <strong class="tool">Bio Builder</strong> with that artist.</p>
<p>A session player counts when they're credited on albums by at least 8 different artists and have no tracks of their own in the library. Change the number in <span class="ui-button">See who</span> (<strong>Credited with at least</strong>, then <span class="ui-button">Update</span> or press Enter). MetaForge remembers it.</p>

<h3>What's waiting?</h3>
<p>The MusicBrainz count is updated each time you open <strong class="tool">MusicBrainz Submit</strong>.</p>

<h3>Changing the layout</h3>
<p>Which tiles show, how wide they are and their order are set in <strong>Settings › Dashboard</strong>:</p>
<ol>
    <li>Tick the tiles to show, and choose how many columns wide each one is.</li>
    <li>Change the order with <span class="ui-button">Move up</span> and <span class="ui-button">Move down</span>, or drag a tile by its handle (<span aria-hidden="true">⠿</span> on the left). Press Escape while dragging to cancel.</li>
    <li>Choose <span class="ui-button">Save dashboard</span>. <span class="ui-button">Reset to default</span> puts the original layout back in the list (choose Save dashboard to keep it).</li>
</ol>
<p class="note">When text is enlarged, wide tiles take fewer columns so nothing runs off the screen.</p>

<h3>Adding and removing tiles</h3>
<p>Each tile is its own small plug-in, in a folder of its own under <code>tools\dashboard\tiles\</code>, just as each tool has its own folder under <code>tools\</code>. A new tile's folder is found by itself and shows up at the end of the Dashboard and in Settings. Deleting a tile's folder removes it.</p>
<!-- --- END OF FILE help.mfi --- -->
